course: dictionary
lesson: 3469
title: Loyal and true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Faithful means loyal and true. A faithful friend stays with you and supports you, even when things are hard. «The Rat goes back to his faithful old river, which never packs up, moves house or goes away for the winter.» The river is always there, so faithful means it never leaves.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego refused to bow to a golden statue and said they would stay faithful even if God did not rescue them.» They refused to bow, even though it was risky, so staying faithful means keeping true to what they believe. Check your meaning by swapping in loyal: "stay loyal even if..." still makes sense.
explain: Faithful can also mean exact. A "faithful copy" is a true copy of the original. The faithful, with "the" in front, means people who keep their faith, often in church. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence best.
fact: Faithful means loyal and true, always staying with and supporting a person, a team or a promise.
fact: «Faithful» can also mean exact and true to the original, as in «a faithful copy».
fact: «The faithful» means believers, people who firmly believe in God and keep their faith.
fact: A faithful husband or wife is loyal to their partner and does not love someone else.
fact: «Faithful» is an adjective, so its comparative form is «more faithful».
exercise: «The Rat goes back to his faithful old river.» What does faithful mean here? | Full of fish | Muddy and cold | Far away | *Loyal and always there
exercise: «Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego said they would stay faithful.» What does stay faithful mean? | Forget their promises | Sing loudly | Leave quickly | *Keep true to their beliefs, even when it is hard
exercise: A teacher says the copy is «a faithful copy» of the painting. What does faithful mean? | *Exact and true to the original | Angry | Very loud | Very old
test: What is a faithful friend? | One who always wins games | One who never speaks | *One who stays loyal and supports you | One who lives far away
test: In church, what does «the faithful» mean? | Old buildings | *People who firmly believe in God | People who are always late | People who sing very badly
exam: Which sentence uses faithful to mean loyal? | The faithful were all sent home early | The faithful copy was sent to the printer | *The dog waited by the gate every single day for his owner | Old Faithful is a geyser in the USA
